    "number": 36014,
    "state": "open",
    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "init: ignore repeated `-addnode` startup values",
    "user": {
      "login": "w0xlt",
      "id": 94266259,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBZ5jkw",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94266259?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/w0xlt",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Startup `-addnode` values are copied directly into the connection manager's added-node list. Unlike runtime `addnode add` calls, this path does not reject repeated values.\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n\r\n```\r\n-addnode=example.com\r\n-addnode=example.com\r\n```\r\n\r\nBoth entries are currently stored. While the destination is disconnected, `ThreadOpenAddedConnections()` processes\r\neach entry during every retry cycle. \r\n\r\nThis can cause redundant DNS lookups, connection attempts, and log messages. `getaddednodeinfo` also reports the repeated entry.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis change is complementary to, and independent of, #35600.\r\n\r\n#35600 prevents overlapping manual connection attempts by tracking destinations while a connection attempt is in progress. \r\nThis PR instead removes repeated `-addnode` values before the connection threads start, preventing duplicate stored entries and sequential redundant retries.\r\n\r\nIt does not replace or broaden #35600's in-flight connection handling.",
